C2  default confirmation count -- loop.py:94-106 (_confirm_runs)
========================================================================
  104: return max(0, int(os.environ.get("FLUIDFIX_CONFIRM", "1")))
    FLUIDFIX_CONFIRM=None   -> _confirm_runs()=1
    FLUIDFIX_CONFIRM=0      -> _confirm_runs()=0
    FLUIDFIX_CONFIRM=1      -> _confirm_runs()=1
    FLUIDFIX_CONFIRM=3      -> _confirm_runs()=3
    FLUIDFIX_CONFIRM=junk   -> _confirm_runs()=1
  outcome: 0 disables the HIDDEN lane entirely (loop.py:357 `and _confirm_runs()`),
  so a one-run green is SHIPped -- the lane that dropped the measured
  14% false-accept rate to 0 is switched off by an env var.

========================================================================
C3  file_share escalation cap -- guard.py:591-592
========================================================================
  589: # one file gets at most half the escalation budget (adversarial
  590: # review, 2026-08-31 — depth-first starvation)
  591: file_share = ((deadline - time.time()) / 2
  592: if total_deadline is not None else escalate_budget / 2)
  596: deadline=min(deadline,
  597: time.time() + file_share))
  outcome: caps ONE file's escalation slice. Two different formulas:
    --budget given      -> (remaining wall clock) / 2
    --budget not given  -> escalate_budget / 2  (a CONSTANT 300s,
                           independent of how much clock is left)
  escalate_budget default = 600
  Divergence, measured by substitution (no clock consumed):
      0s spent, 600s left: budget-mode share=300.0s   no-budget-mode share=300.0s
    300s spent, 300s left: budget-mode share=150.0s   no-budget-mode share=300.0s
    550s spent,  50s left: budget-mode share= 25.0s   no-budget-mode share=300.0s   <- exceeds the clock left

